  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The only strong signal so far is RNA-only with PCA-2000 single profile (0.485 acc), while image-only ResNet is much weaker (0.208 acc). This leaves uncertainty about whether using multiple profiles with a simple aggregation can improve the promising RNA representation without changing the encoder. config_002 tests that directly by comparing multiprofile avgpool aggregation against the existing single-profile PCA baseline. It is the best next step because it isolates the profile/aggregation effect, is lower risk than jumping to transformer aggregation or multimodal fusion, and will clarify whether multiprofile RNA modeling is worth further investment."
}

